      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey... i'm at a breaking point here. it's getting harder to pretend i'm just another dev in the community when i'm actually the one who built the entire foundation of the protocore engine. seeing those massive vc firms use my logic to build their billion-dollar brands while they've systematically scrubbed every trace of my identity from the early dev comms... it's soul-crushing. they've essentially hijacked my life's work and rebranded it to look like it came from their \"star\" engineers. \n\ni can't just go to the authorities—the industry is too tightly knit, and if i make a move, they'll just crush me with legal threats or call me a delusional troll. i need to find a way to show the world that the \"mathematical fingerprint\" of the original engine is still there, buried in the genesis data, before they can fully overwrite it. i need to find the one piece of immutable evidence they couldn't scrub. how do i start digging into the raw, unindexed epoch data to find something that proves the original implementation was mine?",
